name c01m09-valley-of-instant-death
timeout 600
time 1992-10-29T07:48:00Z

# COMANCHE: MAXIMUM OVERKILL (NovaLogic 1992), CAMPAIGN ONE "OPERATION MAXIMUM OVERKILL",
# MISSION 9 OF 10 -- {Valley of Instant Death}* [MIS].
# Spec, provenance and every open question: mods/comanche/doc/campaign.md, terrain.md,
# substitutions.md, hud.md. Format: doc/missions/syntax.md.
#
# THE TASK [MIS]: 16 goals -- 4 T-80s, 4 fuel tanks and 8 Geckos -- alone, with 14 Hellfires for
# 16 targets. The arithmetic is deliberately short and the briefing says why: "we accentally told all
# the news stations where you would be and sold the enemy a few truck loads of guided missles."
#
# THE FIELD [MIS]: map 4 (Khash Rud, Afghanistan, terrain.md 6), day -- sun +44.51 deg at the
# lead's spawn, computed by the runner. 16 starred objects, unlock marker *.
# THE CAST: 6 Werewolf -> `ah64` - 4 T-80 -> `target_hard` - 4 fuel tank -> `target_soft` - 8
# Gecko -> `sa8`.
# THE LOADOUT [MIS]: cannon 500, rockets 62, Hellfire 14, Stinger 2, artillery 5, wingman 0, fuel
# 10000. Declared here: 4 x `mk82`, 2 x `aim9`, gun 500, `set fuel_int_pct 50` = 10000 against the
# campaign's own maximum of 20 000. The rockets and the artillery have no row and no mechanism;
# the truncation of the other two is the F-16's nine pylons.

# ---- THE SEVEN DISCLOSURES ARE STATED IN FULL IN c01m01-werewolves-on-patrol.fbm AND APPLY HERE
# ---- UNCHANGED: D1 no rotorcraft (the RAH-66 flies as `module f16`, 300 kt because 180-275 kt crash
# ---- the egress) - D2 the Werewolf is an `ah64` mover and fires nothing, ever - D3 flat 0 m ground,
# ---- because one mod carries one DEM and this campaign needs four theatres - D4 the clock is checked
# ---- against the logged sun elevation - D5 the anchoring is terrain.md's reconstruction and the
# ---- campaign names no place - D6 the striker spawns on the bearing to its aim point, because the
# ---- attack phase cannot fly itself onto its own run-in - D7 one striker is one aim point.
#
# READING RULE (binding). The verdict is `lead`'s, and it flies ALONE.
#   SUCCESS/exit 0 requires the 16 ground goals with 14 Hellfires -- deliberately two short, so a win
#   is only a win if the shortfall was covered by cannon or rockets, and telemetry must say which.
#   MEASURED: the question cannot be put. The F-16 has nine pylons, so 14 Hellfires truncate to four
#   `mk82`; there is no rocket row in this tree at all; and D7 caps the sortie at one release. The
#   campaign's sharpest arithmetic constraint is unreachable from below, not from above.
#   exit 3 = the expected reading; report the met count against 16.

# MEASURED (exit 3, `--elev const`): ONE OF SIXTEEN -- the campaign's worst ratio, and the mission
#   whose own premise is arithmetic.
#   t = 21.4 s          one Mk-82 away, aimErrM 4.61; f04 destroyed
#   verdict             `lead` TIMEOUT, 1 of 16 met, `survive` met. 48 SA-8 launches, no hit.
#   14 Hellfires declared by the game, 4 `mk82` carried, 1 released.

unit lead
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight m09 1
  spawn 31.75750 62.97546 150 316.5 300
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 50
  set datalink on
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 mk82
  set store 4 mk82
  set store 6 mk82
  set store 7 mk82
  set store 1 aim9
  set store 2 aim9
  set gun_rounds 500
  set cmds_mode auto
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  wp 31.79278 62.93605 150 300
  wp 31.81678 62.90923 1000 300
  objective kill unit t01
  objective kill unit t02
  objective kill unit t03
  objective kill unit t04
  objective kill unit g01
  objective kill unit g02
  objective kill unit g03
  objective kill unit g04
  objective kill unit g05
  objective kill unit g06
  objective kill unit g07
  objective kill unit g08
  objective kill unit f01
  objective kill unit f02
  objective kill unit f03
  objective kill unit f04
  objective survive

